From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero: add i2c aliases

The I2C core numbers adapters after the "i2cN" aliases and hands out
dynamic numbers in probe order to adapters without one. The Orange Pi
Zero2/Zero3 DT declares no i2c aliases, so a TWI enabled by an overlay
gets whatever number is free when it probes (the DesignWare HDMI DDC
adapter takes one too): TWI3 on header pins 3/5 does not show up as
/dev/i2c-3, and the bus number changes with the set of enabled buses.
Scripts, the overlay documentation and the vendor manual all name the
buses i2c-0..i2c-5 after the controller.

Pin the numbering as the vendor BSP does (sun50iw9p1.dtsi twi0..twi5,
twi5 = R_TWI): i2c0..i2c4 = TWI0..TWI4, i2c5 = R_TWI. Disabled nodes
get no adapter, so nothing changes for buses that stay off; the HDMI
DDC adapter now numbers from 6.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 / {
 	aliases {
 		ethernet0 = &emac0;
+		i2c0 = &i2c0;
+		i2c1 = &i2c1;
+		i2c2 = &i2c2;
+		i2c3 = &i2c3;
+		i2c4 = &i2c4;
+		i2c5 = &r_i2c;
 		mmc0 = &mmc0; /* microSD slot */
 		mmc1 = &mmc1; /* SDIO WiFi/BT module */
 		serial0 = &uart0;
-- 
Armbian

